  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Night blindness is developed due to deficiency of vitamin-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p><p>Vitamin A deficiency leads to a disease known as night blindness.&nbsp;People with night blindness have a normal vision when adequate light is present&nbsp;but poor vision in the dark.</p><p>Vitamin A is necessary for the production of retinal, a component of rhodopsin.&nbsp;</p>"
